# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'Registrar: add deregister flow'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      Adds deregistration to the registrar pallets, the counterpart of the register flow and
      with the same shape: the parachain asks, the relay chain answers, and only the answer
      moves money.

      `pallet-registrar-para::deregister` is callable by the manager, the para itself or root. A
      merely reserved id is dropped on the spot with its deposit returned. A registered para must
      leave the relay chain's registry too, so the entry parks as `Deregistering` and the relay
      chain's verdict settles it: confirmation releases both deposits, refusal puts it back to
      registered. A verdict that never arrives is chased up with `cancel_deregistration` after
      `PendingDeadline`, mirroring `cancel_registration`.

      A para that still holds a coretime lease or region cannot be deregistered out from under
      itself. The new `AssignmentChecker` config type answers that; `()` never blocks, for
      runtimes without coretime knowledge. There is also a new `ParachainOrigin` config type so
      a para can act as itself.

      On the relay side, `pallet-registrar-relay::deregister` checks the manager and the lock and
      removes the para, reporting refusals back instead of erroring so the parachain never sits on
      stuck deposits. An id the registry never knew is confirmed as gone rather than refused. The
      `ParachainRegistrar` trait grows `manager_of`, `is_locked` and `deregister`, implemented by
      `paras_registrar`.

      Still not wired into a production runtime.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: minor
